<h1>Dimensioning</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">T</span><span lang="EN-US">he</span> <span lang="EN-US" class="Command">Dimensioning</span> <span class="Command">mode</span> <span lang="EN-US">command is accessible from</span> <b><i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Measure &gt; Dimensioning</b></span></i></b> <span lang="EN-US">or by pressing</span> <b><i style="font-weight:normal; font-style:normal;"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Dimensioning mode</b></span> button</i></b> in the toolbar.</p>
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b> <span lang="EN-US">This command switches the mode for creating and editing dimensions. For the moment dimensions in KUBE represent distances between two points. Points can be picked from vertices of compound entities or from feature points of datums &#160;In this mode a <u><a href="../User_Interface/Measure_Context_Menus.htm#Viewport_Dimensions">context menu</a></u> appears when clicking on a dimension with the RMB, offering all functions associated to the dimension editing.</span></p>
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">The cursor changes to dimension tool <img src="../Measure/images/dimension_mode_cursor.gif" width="32px" height="32px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""> for 3D dimensions and <img src="../Measure/images/dimension_mode_cursorX.gif" width="32px" height="32px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt="">, <img src="../Measure/images/dimension_mode_cursorY.gif" width="32px" height="32px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt="">, or <img src="../Measure/images/dimension_mode_cursorZ.gif" width="32px" height="32px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""> for 1D dimensions. Click on a point from compound entity (scan data, mesh, point cloud, probe points, polyline) or feature point of a datum (line start point, sphere centre, etc.), from where the dimension line starts. Then click on a point where the dimension line ends. While holding the left mouse button move the mouse cursor to the position where you want to place the dimension. Hold down the</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">key if you want to directly create 1D dimension.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a4"><span lang="EN-US" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Dimensions example</u></span></a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP223847677" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Measure/images/dimensioning.gif" width="912px" height="685px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Dimensions consist of line with arrows in both ends, value in the centre of the line, and two limiting lines. If fitted the value is in the centre of the dimension line, otherwise it is automatically carried on left, top, or bottom of the line depending on the particular situation.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a3"><span lang="EN-US" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Example</u></span></a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP236144934" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Measure/images/dimension_values.gif" width="166px" height="74px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""><br>
<br>
Dimension value within the line (top) and outside the line (bottom)</p>
</div>
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US"><a name="Dimension_types"></a>Dimensions can be:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>3D</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">- the absolute distance between the two picked points in 3D space.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>2D</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">- projection of the dimension line on OXY, OYZ, or OXZ plane of the co-ordinate system.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>1D</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">- projection of the dimension line on OX, OY, or OZ axis of the co-ordinate system.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1"><span lang="EN-US" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Dimensions schematic</u></span></a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP168841184" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Measure/images/dimension_schematic.gif" width="488px" height="451px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt="">`</p>
</div>
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">When you pass over the value of an existing dimension line the cursor changes its shape to <img src="../Measure/images/hand_cursor.gif" width="22px" height="26px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""> To modify dimension line position, just click on it and drag the line to the position you want. Hold down</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">key to make it 1D in X or Y, or in Y or Z, or in X or Z depending on the viewport orientation.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2"><span lang="EN-US" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Move dimension example</u></span></a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP289807225" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Measure/images/move_dimension.gif" width="183px" height="291px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:normal;"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:normal;">Dimensions can be formatted individually or all at once. To format individual dimension right-click on it and from the context menu select <a href="Modify_(Dimensions).htm">Modify</a> command. To format all dimensions go to</span> <span style="font-style:italic;"><i><a href="Preferences_-_Display_-_Dimensions.htm">Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Dimensions</a></i></span> <span class="Command" style="font-weight:normal;">dialog.</span></b></p>
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:normal;"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:normal;">Dimensions can be deleted individually or all at once. To delete individual dimension right-click on it and from the context menu select <a href="Delete_Dimension.htm">Delete Dimension</a> command. To delete all dimensions in the s</span><span class="Command" style="font-weight:normal;">cene</span></b> <b><span class="Command" style="font-weight:normal;">right-click on a dimension value and from the context menu select</span> <span class="Command"><a href="delete_all_dimensions.htm" style="font-weight:bold;">Delete All Dimensions</a></span></b> command or go to Measure menu and select the same command from there.</p>
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Command"><b style="font-weight:normal;">When rotate the scene dimensions are always orientated parallel to the line connecting the two picked points or to the axes of the co-ordinate system - depending on the dimension type.</b></span></p>
<p class="Note" id="P2"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: When an entity (or both entities) is used for dimensioning is hid then all dimensions related to that entity (entities) are also hid.</b></p>
<p class="Warning"><b style="font-weight:normal;">Dimensions and their positions are stored in the sab2 file so next time you open it all created dimensions appear. Formatting is not stored so when you open the file, the dimensions will be formatted with their default settings.</b></p>
